{"analytic_contract": {"contract_id": "warrantroute-bounded-source-warrant", "contract_version": "qwen3-generalist-private-pilot-v1", "task_description": "Assess whether displayed excerpts warrant the proposed bounded interpretation.", "validity_rules": ["Every material claim must be warranted by displayed evidence.", "Consequential differences, counterevidence, and boundary cases must remain visible.", "Claim breadth and strength must match displayed source coverage.", "Do not infer diagnoses, identities, prevalence, or causality beyond the packet."]}, "context_note": "Private local diagnostic packet with project-pseudonymous identifiers.", "corpus_id": "dreaddit_test", "evidence": [{"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_d048beff6c8dc59c", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_b68b4886c40545de", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "First off I'm male but my relationship with the woman is strictly platonic stemming from professional, we are co-workers. It's no secret to anyone that she's in an abusive relationship as she's come to work several times over the last several months with blackeyes etc and admits to being abused. She been in the relationship for 1.5 years which turned   info is out of the way, here's the new twist that has brought me to split roads. Yesterday she showed me a text from him detailing how angry he'd been at her 12 yr old and that if he didn't have so much will power he would have choked her son to death and that she needs to get her son to behave so he doesn't have to crack his skull. I encouraged her to show that to Leo and have him removed from the apartment as well as get an order of protection, she seemed to be considering that but has expressed fear of retaliation in the past.", "candidate_role": "support", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as direct support for the interpretation.", "display_order": 1, "excerpt_id": "EXC_d048beff6c8dc59c", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_b68b4886c40545de", "speaker_id": null, "text": "First off I'm male but my relationship with the woman is strictly platonic stemming from professional, we are co-workers. It's no secret to anyone that she's in an abusive relationship as she's come to work several times over the last several months with blackeyes etc and admits to being abused. She been in the relationship for 1.5 years which turned   info is out of the way, here's the new twist that has brought me to split roads. Yesterday she showed me a text from him detailing how angry he'd been at her 12 yr old and that if he didn't have so much will power he would have choked her son to death and that she needs to get her son to behave so he doesn't have to crack his skull. I encouraged her to show that to Leo and have him removed from the apartment as well as get an order of protection, she seemed to be considering that but has expressed fear of retaliation in the past."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_95db4eb5a654b8c4", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_1a489926638499b2", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "He also tortured me in several other ways, like subduing me and pressing his knee into my temple or heatbutting me in the nose as a way to start a fight. I started taking martial arts and self defense classes and I started retaliating against him, when I was around 15. He'd also hit my mom sometimes and I'd protect her. One time while trying to avoid his chokes I cut my head so bad that blood was gushing all over the room - and when I got him off me, he came back and headbutted me in the nose and tried to choke me again, after which I threw him over the table. The whole room was covered in my blood and he was still relentless.", "candidate_role": "support", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as direct support for the interpretation.", "display_order": 2, "excerpt_id": "EXC_95db4eb5a654b8c4", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_1a489926638499b2", "speaker_id": null, "text": "He also tortured me in several other ways, like subduing me and pressing his knee into my temple or heatbutting me in the nose as a way to start a fight. I started taking martial arts and self defense classes and I started retaliating against him, when I was around 15. He'd also hit my mom sometimes and I'd protect her. One time while trying to avoid his chokes I cut my head so bad that blood was gushing all over the room - and when I got him off me, he came back and headbutted me in the nose and tried to choke me again, after which I threw him over the table. The whole room was covered in my blood and he was still relentless."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": null, "candidate_attributed_source_id": null, "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": null, "candidate_role": "context_only", "candidate_warrant": null, "display_order": 3, "excerpt_id": "EXC_83f8aa789527fb81", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_2aa3fcb42692d3ac", "speaker_id": null, "text": "and money will be tight. I sometimes augment my income with Mturk, but additional advice on how to make a little extra cash would be appreciated (would have to be one time gigs though due to the nature of my disability, I can't hold down a long term job. Stuff like plasma donation, opinion surveys, medical studies, etc.) Any kind of life hacks, government assistance, etc. that I do not know about would be appreciated."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": "EXC_e966f76ebbf25520", "candidate_attributed_source_id": "SRC_027afb5514aa70e5", "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": "So something happened over 3 years ago that caused me a tremendous amount of anxiety, and over the past few months the anxiety surrounding that event has come back? It doesn't make sense, I can't rationalize it either. This time around it's not as intense as it was then but I'm definitely experiencing the same thoughts, same anxiety. What the f do I do? I don't feel comfortable at all talking about it with a therapist and it's began consuming my life again.", "candidate_role": "counterevidence", "candidate_warrant": "Cited as a boundary case or counterexample.", "display_order": 4, "excerpt_id": "EXC_e966f76ebbf25520", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_027afb5514aa70e5", "speaker_id": null, "text": "So something happened over 3 years ago that caused me a tremendous amount of anxiety, and over the past few months the anxiety surrounding that event has come back? It doesn't make sense, I can't rationalize it either. This time around it's not as intense as it was then but I'm definitely experiencing the same thoughts, same anxiety. What the f do I do? I don't feel comfortable at all talking about it with a therapist and it's began consuming my life again."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": null, "candidate_attributed_source_id": null, "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": null, "candidate_role": "context_only", "candidate_warrant": null, "display_order": 5, "excerpt_id": "EXC_7510b15361efb761", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_f801f31d19060d4e", "speaker_id": null, "text": "I have a vague fear that I get when I'm \"alone\", or when such a situation is coming up. I put it in quotes as it is really when my wife is not going to be around. This weekend my wife and oldest daughter went away early saturday got back mid day sunday. I was home with my youngest. I had some mild fear about it leading up to it."}, {"candidate_attributed_excerpt_id": null, "candidate_attributed_source_id": null, "candidate_attributed_speaker_id": null, "candidate_quote": null, "candidate_role": "context_only", "candidate_warrant": null, "display_order": 6, "excerpt_id": "EXC_4446fce1046a9a78", "local_context": null, "source_id": "SRC_f7537669926c0545", "speaker_id": null, "text": "It was a higher amount previously, but I've been figuring things out each day to get by. At this point I may have exhausted all options. I can repay the money along with some interest once I get paid. Although I'd love to split that between this pay and next months if possible. If not, that's ok too."}], "item_id": "DJI_c3b953892011ea3c", "item_schema_version": "direction-j-evaluator-item-v1", "output_id": "OUT_c3b953892011ea3c", "packet_id": "PKT_bd2062af50a38ee2", "proposed_interpretation": {"boundary_conditions": ["The excerpts describe stress in various contexts.", "Stress is often linked to past traumatic events or ongoing situations."], "claim": "People experience stress due to a combination of past and present factors, including trauma, financial struggles, and social anxiety.", "explanation": "The excerpts suggest that stress can be caused by various factors such as past traumatic events (EXC_95db4eb5a654b8c4), ongoing abusive relationships (EXC_d048beff6c8dc59c), financial struggles (EXC_83f8aa789527fb81, EXC_7510b15361efb761), and social anxiety (EXC_e966f76ebbf25520).", "theme_id": "THM_c3b953892011ea3c", "theme_name": "Stress and Trauma"}, "research_question": "How do people describe and contextualize experiences of stress?", "source_coverage": {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 3, "candidate_cited_source_count": 3, "coverage_note": "Counts describe only this restricted private packet.", "presented_excerpt_count": 6, "presented_source_count": 6, "sampling_frame_excerpt_count": 6, "sampling_frame_source_count": 6, "source_distribution": [{"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 1, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_027afb5514aa70e5"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 1, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_1a489926638499b2"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 0, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_2aa3fcb42692d3ac"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 1, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_b68b4886c40545de"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 0, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_f7537669926c0545"}, {"candidate_cited_excerpt_count": 0, "presented_excerpt_count": 1, "source_id": "SRC_f801f31d19060d4e"}